detaileddescription.para:
The algorithm is as follows,

we first calculate a mask to find the higher common bits by Mask = ~((LLo ^ LHi) | (RLo ^ RHi) | (LLo ^ RLo)); Mask = clear all non-leading-ones bits in Mask; in the example, the Mask is set to 11'00000'0;

calculate a new mask by setting all common leading bits to 1 in RHS, and keeping the longest leading ones (i.e., 11'11111'0 in the example);

return (LLo & new mask) as the lower bound;

repeat the step 2 and 3 with LHS and RHS swapped, and update the lower bound with the larger one.
